          ],
          "text": "Your son found you on the floor after a fall. You had got up to use the commode.\n\nThe team found you had:\n- Sepsis\n- Possible aspiration pneumonia (a possible chest infection from inhaling something)\n- Sigmoid diverticulitis (inflammation in part of your large bowel)\n- Dilated bowel loops, which may mean a blockage, and a build-up of stool\n- Acute kidney injury (a sudden drop in how well your kidneys were working)\n- Raised markers of infection in your blood"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "While you were in hospital, the team:\n- Gave you an antibiotic (Tazocin)\n- Gave you fluids through a drip\n- Gave you oxygen\n- Took blood tests, including blood cultures\n- Did a scan of your head, neck and chest, which showed nothing new or urgent\n- Did a scan of your tummy, which showed the bowel changes and the bowel inflammation\n- Did an X-ray of your chest\n- Did an X-ray of your tummy, which showed the dilated bowel loops and build-up of stool\n- Tested your urine\n- Started an Amber care plan"
        },
